<%# One notification row — faithful port of the legacy SPA `Notifications/card.js`.
    Left border colored read/unread; a category-specific Lucide icon + copy; the body
    is a PATCH button (mark read, then redirect to whatever the row is about — the
    DEBATE when one is attached, else the hoojah, else back to the notifications list;
    see the precedence note on `NotificationsController#update`); a trash button DELETEs
    it (Turbo-Stream removes this card). Locals: notification.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.4) —
    docs/design-system/components/social/NotificationCard.prompt.md: "same 8px-left-border
    shape as a compact hoojah card, but the border encodes read state instead of stance."
    That is why `DesignSystemHelper::CARD_STANCES` is six values and not three — `read`
    and `unread` are in the set for this file alone, and `ui/_card`'s `stance:` builds
    `border-<state>` by the same interpolation this partial used to do inline. The two
    colours behind those classes arrived in Task 1.1; before that the border rendered as
    nothing at all, which is what spec/system/design_tokens_spec.rb now pins (it asserts
    the class AND the computed colour, so a lost class and a lost token fail separately).

    The bare Accept / Decline / Mark as read controls take
    `ds_button_classes(variant: :link, ...)`. That variant carries no font size on
    purpose — these sit in a 14px row and an emitted `text-base` would visibly enlarge
    them against it. Tone is the design system's: primary for the affirmative action,
    grey for Decline and for the trash.

    The two `link_to "View profile"` rows and the two body `button_to`s are deliberately
    NOT buttons-by-helper. The body ones are truncating text blocks (`truncate` plus a
    `max-w-[350px]` clamp) and the `:link` variant's `inline-flex` would break the
    overflow they depend on; the "View profile" rows are already plain primary links.

    CATEGORY COVERAGE — both `case`es cover all fourteen `Notification` categories.
    They used to stop at eight, so the four `debate_*` ones (which fire on every
    challenge / decline / your-turn / conclude) plus the two legacy SPA leftovers
    (`admin`, `flag`, which nothing in this codebase creates but which may still
    exist as migrated rows) rendered with no icon and no copy line at all.
    Icon choices: `swords` is the established debate motif here (challenge dialog,
    debate card, debate header); `flag` matches the flagging UI's own uses; `bell`
    matches the notifications empty state in `notifications/index.html.erb`.
    The `else` arms are unreachable today — the enum rejects unknown values, so no
    factory can exercise them. They are insurance for the fifteenth category: a new
    enum value renders a bell and a generic line instead of a blank row.

    FROZEN: `dom_id(notification)` is what `destroy.turbo_stream.erb` removes.
    Every `button_to` path and verb, and `aria-label="Delete notification"`, which
    spec/system/notifications_spec.rb clicks by name. %>
<% read = notification.read? %>
<%= render layout: "ui/card",
      locals: {id: dom_id(notification),
               stance: read ? "read" : "unread",
               class: "pr-2 flex items-center mb-1"} do %>
  <div class="flex items-center py-1 w-full">
    <div class="flex items-center ml-3 fill-grey shrink-0">
      <% case notification.category %>
      <% when "announcement" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("megaphone", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "new_hoojah_response" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("message-circle", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "new_vote" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("bar-chart-3", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "mention" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("at-sign", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "new_follower" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("user-plus", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "follow_request" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("user-plus", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "follow_accepted" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("user-check", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "badge_earned" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("award", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "debate_challenge" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("swords", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "debate_declined" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("x-circle", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "debate_your_turn" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("reply", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "debate_concluded" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("gavel", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "admin" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("shield", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% when "flag" %>
        <%= lucide_icon("flag", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% else %>
        <%= lucide_icon("bell", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col text-sm text-grey pr-1 ml-3 min-w-0">
      <span>
        <% case notification.category %>
        <% when "announcement" %>
          Announcement
        <% when "new_hoojah_response" %>
          @<%= notification.subject_user&.username %> posted a new argument on your hoojah
        <% when "new_vote" %>
          You have a new vote on your hoojah
        <% when "mention" %>
          @<%= notification.subject_user&.username %> mentioned you in a hoojah
        <% when "new_follower" %>
          @<%= notification.subject_user&.username %> started following you
        <% when "follow_request" %>
          @<%= notification.subject_user&.username %> requested to follow you
        <% when "follow_accepted" %>
          @<%= notification.subject_user&.username %> accepted your follow request
        <% when "badge_earned" %>
          You earned the <strong><%= Badge::REGISTRY.dig(notification.body, :name) || "achievement" %></strong> badge
        <% when "debate_challenge" %>
          @<%= notification.subject_user&.username %> challenged you to a debate
        <% when "debate_declined" %>
          @<%= notification.subject_user&.username %> declined your debate challenge
        <% when "debate_your_turn" %>
          It's your turn in your debate with @<%= notification.subject_user&.username %>
        <% when "debate_concluded" %>
          Your debate with @<%= notification.subject_user&.username %> has concluded
        <% when "admin" %>
          You have a message from the Hoojah team
        <% when "flag" %>
          Your hoojah was flagged for review
        <% else %>
          You have a new notification
        <% end %>
      </span>

      <% if notification.category == "announcement" %>
        <%= button_to notification_path(notification), method: :patch,
              class: "text-left p-0 bg-transparent border-0 text-grey truncate no-underline" do %>
          <%= notification.body %>
        <% end %>
      <% elsif notification.hujah && notification.hujah.visible_to?(current_user) %>
        <%# Slice 7b (Gate 9, N-1): only render the hoojah body if the recipient may
            actually see it — a private author's hoojah body must not leak through a
            mention/response notification to a non-follower. %>
        <%= button_to notification_path(notification), method: :patch,
              class: "block text-left p-0 bg-transparent border-0 text-grey truncate no-underline max-w-[350px]" do %>
          <%= format_body(notification.hujah.body) %>
        <% end %>
      <% elsif notification.new_follower? && notification.subject_user %>
        <%= link_to "View profile", profile_path(notification.subject_user.username),
              class: "text-left text-primary no-underline" %>
      <% elsif notification.follow_request? && (req_follow = Follow.find_by(follower_id: notification.subject_user_id, followed_id: notification.user_id)) %>
        <%# Accept/decline the pending request in place (Slice 7b). Both button_to's
            hit /follow_requests/:id; FollowRequestPolicy restricts them to this user. %>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <%= button_to "Accept", follow_request_path(req_follow), method: :patch,
                class: ds_button_classes(variant: :link) %>
          <%= button_to "Decline", follow_request_path(req_follow), method: :delete,
                class: ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey") %>
        </div>
      <% elsif notification.follow_accepted? && notification.subject_user %>
        <%= link_to "View profile", profile_path(notification.subject_user.username),
              class: "text-left text-primary no-underline" %>
      <% else %>
        <%# badge_earned has no hujah/subject_user, and neither do admin, flag, or any
            notification whose hoojah is gated from the recipient by the branch above.
            An `else` rather than a category check, so every card always carries at
            least a mark-read affordance and none of them is stuck unread. %>
        <%= button_to "Mark as read", notification_path(notification), method: :patch,
              class: ds_button_classes(variant: :link) %>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <%= button_to notification_path(notification), method: :delete,
          class: "#{ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey")} ml-auto mr-2",
          aria: {label: "Delete notification"} do %>
      <%= lucide_icon("trash-2", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
